import_legacy.description:
BattMind PyScript installations found in the config folder:
{files}

Choose one to import from (it may have another prefix than **{prefix}**). The settings are used as defaults on the next pages, and the databases (charging history, consumption, prices, solar) are copied on first start. The PyScript files are only read, never changed - both versions can run at the same time.

prices_stromligning.description:
Sensors from the Strømligning integration. The buy price is required; the sell sensors are needed to calculate an accurate sell price.

Strømligning switches its excl. VAT sensors off by default, and a disabled sensor can't be selected here: enable them first under **Settings → Devices & services → Entities** (*Show disabled entities*). The price forecasts also need *Include price forecasts for the next week?* in the Strømligning options.
Disabled in Strømligning now: {stromligning_disabled}

prices_stromligning_tariffs.description:
When selling, tariffs and taxes are removed from the price and the transmission/system tariff and sell fee are added. Leave a field empty to use 0.

The tariff sensors may be disabled in Strømligning, and then they can't be selected here: enable them first under **Settings → Devices & services → Entities** (*Show disabled entities*).
Disabled in Strømligning now: {stromligning_disabled}

solar.description:
Optional. With solar, BattMind predicts the surplus that charges the battery for free, can move solar charging to cheaper hours and accumulates `sensor.{prefix}_kwh_charged_by_solar`. Leave empty without solar.

Solcast switches the forecast sensors of day 3 and on off by default: enable them under **Settings → Devices & services → Entities** (*Show disabled entities*) and turn on *Hourly detail* under *Forecast attributes breakdown* in the Solcast options, or those days are planned without Solcast.
Disabled Solcast sensors now: {solcast_disabled}

