stromligning_entities.description:
BattMind ({prefix}) uses Strømligning sensors that are disabled or that Strømligning does not provide. A missing sell tariff counts as 0, which makes the calculated sell price too high, and without the price sensors the stored prices are used.

Disabled in Home Assistant (Strømligning disables its excl. VAT sensors by default – enable them under **Settings → Devices & services → Entities**, with *Show disabled entities*):
{disabled}

Not provided by Strømligning (e.g. the price forecasts are off in its options):
{not_provided}

This repair disappears by itself when the sensors work again.

solcast_entities.description:
BattMind ({prefix}) can't use all the Solcast forecast sensors it needs, so the days without one are planned from the weather forecast and the stored solar history instead. Solcast disables the forecast sensors of day 3 and on by default.

Disabled in Home Assistant (enable them under **Settings → Devices & services → Entities**, with *Show disabled entities*):
{disabled}

Not named the way BattMind expects (the entity id must end in _today, _tomorrow or _day_3 …):
{renamed}

Without hourly detail (turn on *Hourly detail* under *Forecast attributes breakdown* in the Solcast options):
{no_detail}

This repair disappears by itself when the sensors are fixed.
